      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "STANZA I.—The first line forms a compound which may be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "analysed in two ways, (a) as consisting of three adjectives दिका-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "लाद्यनवच्छिन्न, अनन्त and चिन्मात्रमूर्ति, or (b) as a Bahuvrîhi with मूर्ति as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "its second member, and all that precedes मूर्ति as the first, that pre-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "ceding member being itself a compound of three adjectives.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "The substantial meaning is the same in both cases. The com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "mentary seems to take the former of the two modes.[*] दिक्काल=",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "space and time. आदि seems to refer to गुण, धर्माधर्म &c. Compare S'â-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "rîraka Bhâshya (Bibl. Ind. Ed.) p. 64 and gloss of Govind Ânanda",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "thereon (p. 65), both of which are excerpted below. अनवच्छिन्न=",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "unaffected, undefined, or to render it by an equally philosophical",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "term, unconditioned. The commentator says दशदिशासु तथा भूतभवि-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "ष्यद्वर्तमानत्रिकालेषु च अनवच्छिन्नः अत एव अनन्तः. अवच्छिन्न seems here to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "understood as meaning “divided”. But the meaning adopted",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "by us is closer to the philosophical acceptation, and that is a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "reason for adopting it in such a passage as that before us. Thus",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 20,
          "text": "in the passage from S'ankara above alluded to, it is said यत्र धर्मा-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 21,
          "text": "धर्मौ सह कार्येण कालत्रयं च नोपावर्तेते and Govind Ânanda opens his com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 22,
          "text": "ment on it thus कालानवच्छिन्नत्वाच्चेत्याह कालेति. For the idea may be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 23,
          "text": "compared Gregory Nyssen’s description of the Divine Nature",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 24,
          "text": "quoted by the late Mr. Mansel in his Philosophy of the Conditioned",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 25,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 26,
          "text": "(p. 16). “It is neither in place nor in time, but before these and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 27,
          "text": "above these in an unspeakable manner, contemplated itself by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 28,
          "text": "itself, through faith alone, neither measured by ages, nor moving",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
